  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "fcrepo-client-messaging provides a library to allow consumption of Fedora's JMS messages.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "As such one would expect to use it outside of Fedora.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However it has dependencies on fcrepo-server and fcrepo-common; which means a lot of dependent libraries.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It should be possible to remove most of these dependences (eg, see the implementation in the MediaShelf Java client - ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/tree/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/client/messaging)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/tree/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/client/messaging)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
