  "description": "<p>fcrepo-client-messaging provides a library to allow consumption of Fedora's JMS messages.</p>\n\n<p>As such one would expect to use it outside of Fedora.</p>\n\n<p>However it has dependencies on fcrepo-server and fcrepo-common; which means a lot of dependent libraries.</p>\n\n<p>It should be possible to remove most of these dependences (eg, see the implementation in the MediaShelf Java client - <a href=\"https://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/tree/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/client/messaging\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/mediashelf/fedora-client/tree/master/src/main/java/com/yourmediashelf/fedora/client/messaging</a>)</p>",
